---
title: Command line
description: Run KoboldCpp without the launcher. Basic commands for Windows, Linux and macOS, the most-used flags, headless modes and exit codes.
sidebar:
  order: 5
---

Everything in the launcher is also a command-line flag. Use the command line to start KoboldCpp from a script, on a server without a screen, or with a screen reader (the launcher is not accessible to screen readers).

## Start with a model

When you pass a model, KoboldCpp skips the launcher and starts right away.

{% tabs syncKey="os" %}
{% tabitem label="Windows" %}

```sh {% title="Command Prompt" frame="terminal" %}
cd C:\mystuff
koboldcpp.exe --model C:\models\mymodel.gguf --contextsize 16384
```

{% /tabitem %}
{% tabitem label="Linux" %}

```sh {% title="Terminal" frame="terminal" %}
./koboldcpp-linux-x64 --model mymodel.gguf --contextsize 16384
```

{% /tabitem %}
{% tabitem label="macOS" %}

```sh {% title="Terminal" frame="terminal" %}
./koboldcpp-mac-arm64 --model mymodel.gguf --contextsize 16384
```

{% /tabitem %}
{% /tabs %}

Use the name of the file you downloaded, for example `koboldcpp-nocuda.exe` or `./koboldcpp-linux-x64-nocuda`. Examples on other pages write `koboldcpp` for it.

When the model is loaded, the terminal shows `Please connect to custom endpoint at http://localhost:5001`. Open that address in your browser, or add `--launch` to open it automatically.

Other ways to start without the launcher:

- `--config mysettings.kcpps` starts with a saved config. See [Config files](/docs/settings/config-files/).
- `--model` also accepts a web address; KoboldCpp downloads the file first.
- The model file and port also work without flag names: `koboldcpp.exe mymodel.gguf 5002`.

## Get help

| Command | What it does |
|---|---|
| `--help` | Lists all flags with a short description. |
| `--version` | Prints the version and exits. It only works on its own; with other flags it is ignored. |

The [flag reference](/docs/reference/flags/) explains every flag in detail.

## Most-used flags

| Flag | Launcher | What it does |
|---|---|---|
| [`--model`](/docs/reference/flags/#model) | **GGUF Text Model:** | The model file or web address. |
| [`--config`](/docs/reference/flags/#config) | **Load Config** | Loads a `.kcpps` config or `.kcppt` template. |
| [`--contextsize`](/docs/reference/flags/#contextsize) | **Context Size:** | Context size in tokens. Default 16384. |
| [`--usecuda`](/docs/reference/flags/#usecuda) | **Backend:** Use CUDA | Runs on an NVIDIA card. |
| [`--usevulkan`](/docs/reference/flags/#usevulkan) | **Backend:** Use Vulkan | Runs on most graphics cards. |
| [`--usecpu`](/docs/reference/flags/#usecpu) | **Backend:** Use CPU | Runs without a graphics card. On macOS, also set `--gpulayers 0`. |
| [`--gpulayers`](/docs/reference/flags/#gpulayers) | **GPU Layers:** | Layers on the graphics card. `-1` (default) fits automatically. |
| [`--threads`](/docs/reference/flags/#threads) | **Threads:** | CPU threads. Automatic by default. |
| [`--port`](/docs/reference/flags/#port) | **Port:** | Default 5001. |
| [`--host`](/docs/reference/flags/#host) | **Host:** | Address to listen on. Default: all addresses. `127.0.0.1` allows only this computer. |
| [`--launch`](/docs/reference/flags/#launch) | **Launch Browser** | Opens the browser after loading. Off on the command line, on in the launcher. |
| [`--password`](/docs/reference/flags/#password) | **Password:** | API key for the text endpoints. |
| [`--quantkv`](/docs/reference/flags/#quantkv) | **Quantize KV Cache:** | Stores the context in a smaller format. |
| [`--mmproj`](/docs/reference/flags/#mmproj) | **Mmproj File:** | Vision projector for image input. |
| [`--quiet`](/docs/reference/flags/#quiet) | **Quiet Mode** | Hides generation output. |
| [`--debugmode`](/docs/reference/flags/#debugmode) | **Debug Mode** | Prints extra details for troubleshooting. |

Without `--usecuda`, `--usevulkan` or `--usecpu`, KoboldCpp chooses a backend for your hardware.

{% aside type="tip" title="Use the full flag names" %}
Many flags also have short llama.cpp-style names, such as `-c` for `--contextsize` or `-ngl` for `--gpulayers`. Together with `--config`, only the full names override the config's values; see [Config files](/docs/settings/config-files/#change-one-setting-from-the-command-line).
{% /aside %}

## Passwords from environment variables

Passwords can also be set as environment variables instead of flags:

| Variable | Same as |
|---|---|
| `KCPP_PASSWORD` | `--password` |
| `KCPP_ADMINPASSWORD` | `--adminpassword` |

## Modes without the web server

| Flag | What it does |
|---|---|
| `--cli` | Chat with the model in the terminal. Type `/quit` or `/exit` to end. With `--agent`, it runs the KoboldCpp Agent in the terminal instead, and the web server starts as usual. Cannot be combined with `--launch`, `--nomodel`, `--admin` or `--benchmark`. |
| `--prompt "text"` | Generates one reply to the text, prints it and exits. With `--cli`, the text becomes the system prompt instead. |
| `--benchmark` | Measures prompt processing and generation speed instead of starting the server. `--benchmark results.csv` appends the results to a file. |

The opposite also exists: `--nomodel` starts the web server and KoboldAI Lite without a local model, for use with online services.

## Showing or skipping the launcher

- `--showgui` opens the launcher filled in with the flags and config you passed, instead of starting right away.
- `--skiplauncher` cancels a `showgui` setting saved in a config. It does not replace a model: without one, KoboldCpp still asks for a file. On a system without a screen, it prints `Note: In order to use --skiplauncher, you need to specify a model with --model` and exits.

If you pass flags but no model, KoboldCpp shows a file picker for a model or `.kcpps` file instead of the full launcher.

## Exit codes

| Code | When |
|---|---|
| `0` | `--version` printed the version. |
| `1` | The port is already in use (`no socket could bind`). This happens after the model has loaded. |
| `2` | A flag or value is invalid, for example a context size outside 256 to 524288. |
| `2` | The model file does not exist (`Cannot find text model file`). |
| `2` | `--skiplauncher` without a model, on a system without a screen. |

